<!--
    Objective-C metadata of a dyld shared cache image (Noelo-Lab/kuna#1623).

    Issue: in an image loaded from a cache the `objc` pass recovered nothing. A
    cache's small method lists hold their selectors (`0x40000000`) and type
    strings (`0x20000000`) as offsets from the cache's selector base, and carry
    the uniqued and sorted flags in the two low bits of `entsizeAndFlags`; the
    strings and the `__objc_selrefs` targets live in libobjc's `__OBJC_RO`
    region outside the image; `class_ro_t.baseMethods` with its low bit set is
    a relative list of lists.

    Fix: `loader/kuna_dyldcache.rs` finds the selector base in the cache
    header's ObjCOptimizationHeader, else in libobjc's `objc_opt_t`
    (`__objc_opt_ro`, version 16); `analyzers/objc/kuna_objccache.rs` reads
    addresses outside the image through the cache; `methods.rs` decodes the
    flags; `classt.rs` walks the list of lists.

    `dyld_cache_objc.py` builds two caches with one stripped `libgreeter.dylib`
    (no symbols at all) and a `libobjc.A.dylib` owning the strings: the first
    with the ObjCOptimizationHeader, the `_v16` one without it (its header
    ends before `objcOptsOffset`), so the fallback is what finds the base.

    Pass 1 (`objc off`): the IMP is `sub_180001800`. Pass 2 and 3 (`objc on`,
    each cache): `int -[Greeter greet:](Greeter *self,objc_selector *_cmd,int arg1)`
    from the type string `i24@0:8i16`. Pass 2 also shows `-[Greeter count]`,
    the `objc_msgSend$count` stub typed from it, and `-[Greeter shout]`, a
    preattached category method whose IMP is in libobjc, named as an import.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
